{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"root","type":"text","text":"# GOAL — find the counter-team\nSearch the VGC Reg-M-B space for the team that beats the collected meta. $f$ = win rate vs the 545-team pool, measured by paired battles on local Showdown + poke-env.\nPipeline: **enumerate species → pick sets → battle-policy plays → surrogate predicts $f$ → search loop refines**","x":-720,"y":-300,"width":620,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n🟩 battle policy · 🟦 search methods · 🟧 reading\n🟪 problem frame · 🟨 output/side threads\n↓ solid = prerequisite → unlocked\n⇢ short labelled edge = adjacent-column feed\nCross-references further away are written as *(from …)* inside the node, not drawn — keeps arrows off the text\n✅ done · ⚠ open decision","x":-1950,"y":-300,"width":480,"height":260},
		{"id":"settled","type":"text","text":"## Settled decisions\n- [x] Stack = Showdown + poke-env, Reg M-B, Pikalytics/Limitless\n- [x] Brute force out; species enumeration phase 1, set choice phase 2\n- [x] Surrogate = ridge matchup predictor with pairwise terms\n- [x] Ladder validation = held-out-team generalisation only (VGC-Bench §4.3)\n- [x] ~~Reimplementation rule (2026-08-24)~~ *superseded 2026-08-26 by the sequencing rule*\n- [x] **Sequencing rule (2026-08-24): read ALL HIGH-graded papers first, then reimplement / run experiments, then MED papers — a mid paper never delays a high experiment**","x":1290,"y":-300,"width":560,"height":290,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a1","type":"text","text":"## 🟪 A · Problem frame — *foundations*\n✅ Enumeration, not continuous optimisation — species subsets phase 1, sets phase 2\n✅ Brute force out; slot size ≈ 7.3×10⁷ median — [[Clause or the feature of the search space]]\n✅ Team Preview: 90² opening states (EliteFurret)\n⚠ Weighted-max-cover gap stands (2026-08-19 sweep, 0 HIGH survive)","x":-1950,"y":160,"width":560,"height":230,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a2","type":"text","text":"### The objective $f$ and its surrogate\n✅ $\\tilde f$ = ridge regression, pairwise strength terms — [[Decision — the matchup predictor is ridge with pairwise terms]]\nFeeds the search methods in column C *(edge omitted — see C1)*\n- [ ] Monte Carlo battle budget ([[Monte Carlo battle budget — what 800 battles can resolve]])\n- [ ] Counter-matrix prior — Lin et al. TMLR 2024 (MED)","x":-1950,"y":450,"width":560,"height":230},
		{"id":"a3","type":"text","text":"### ⚠ Blocking open question\n- [ ] Training opponent distribution — uniform over VGCPastes pool recommended, **unconfirmed**; gates the experiment plan →","x":-1950,"y":750,"width":560,"height":130},
		{"id":"b1","type":"text","text":"## 🟩 B · Battle policy — *spine*\n- [ ] **Reimplement VGC-Bench** — run release, reproduce BC → SP/FP/DO, extend on team-pool size\n✅ Cloned `~/code/vgc-bench`, submodule pinned, 545 teams verified","x":-1150,"y":160,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b2","type":"text","text":"- [ ] **Experiment plan write-up** (decided in chat, recorded nowhere else)\nArms BC-init + SP/FP/DO · random baseline · Glicko ranking · beat BC ≥ 60%, no arm beats winner > 55% · 107-way action space + policy-controlled preview\n⚠ child 5 = opponent distribution ← blocked by A3","x":-1150,"y":400,"width":560,"height":190},
		{"id":"b3","type":"text","text":"- [ ] **FootsiesGym arm-ranking harness** — seed-crossed cross-play matrix + best-response exploitability probe (protocol from D5, owner-approved); probe measures, never trains\n- [ ] Seed-plumbing patch (`>start` seed never sent by challenge path) → **blocks** CRN paired battles (Lesson 0006)","x":-1150,"y":660,"width":560,"height":190},
		{"id":"b4","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Action masking — state-dependent legality (fainted slots, Choice lock, disabled moves); penalties suppress valid actions (RLC 2026 Paper 1)\n[[How do you implementing maskout in reinforcement learning and whey do you need to mask out]]\n- [ ] AWBC upgrade — MED verdict, chess-puzzles conversion","x":-1150,"y":930,"width":560,"height":190},
		{"id":"b5","type":"text","text":"- [ ] **PPO vs SAC per arm** — battles cheap + parallel on M4 Pro → PPO leans for SP arm; FP/DO arms (frozen opponents, replay legal): off-policy learner or one algorithm everywhere?","x":-1150,"y":1200,"width":560,"height":150},
		{"id":"b6","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Robust-to-team-styles training — pool stratified by archetype · team-conditioned obs · checkpoint-population opponents · held-out archetypes for Glicko · worst-case win rate = robust metric","x":-1150,"y":1430,"width":560,"height":150},
		{"id":"b7","type":"text","text":"### Infra track — PufferLib\n✅ Pin 3.0.0 decided · - [ ] act-on-findings (child 5: vectorizer-only vs full loop, forfeits `MaskedActorCriticPolicy`) · - [ ] read 5.0 native self-play · - [ ] throughput A/B swap\n[[PufferLib for the battle-policy stack — research findings]]","x":-1150,"y":1660,"width":560,"height":180},
