		{"id":"c1","type":"text","text":"## 🟦 C · Search methods under test\nInput $\\tilde f$ comes from A2 *(written here instead of a long arrow)*\n- [ ] Simulated annealing — noisy-SA menu: Ball/Branke sampling, Gelfand–Mitter 1/T² costing\n- [ ] Bayesian optimisation\n- [ ] Cross-entropy method — best structural fit (factored sampling, noise-tolerant elite update)\n⚠ gate: decision 7 must admit CEM beside SA + BO\n✅ OpenSpiel sweep: nothing usable — verified 2026-08-20","x":-350,"y":160,"width":560,"height":290,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c2","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Quality-diversity — deep-surrogate MAP-Elites prototype (Lesson 0004)\nOpen until run: does fitted $\\tilde f$ earn its training cost? Origin lens: Fontaine 2019 sliding boundaries","x":-350,"y":520,"width":560,"height":160},
		{"id":"c3","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Learned search policy — Q-learning over team-edit actions (Q-DeckRec): amortises re-searches when the meta shifts. Children: formulation · applications · runnable code · /teach lesson","x":-350,"y":750,"width":560,"height":160},
		{"id":"c4","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Pruning rules — **StreamLLM (HIGH)**: LLM-written streamliners validated battle-free; replaces retired ReEvo. Method sources ← D2\n⚠ retention-scoring risk: prunes off-meta counters\nChildren: example rule vs meta list · hard filter vs soft penalty\n- [ ] Hyper-heuristic layer — earns a place beyond pruning?","x":-350,"y":980,"width":560,"height":230},
		{"id":"c5","type":"text","text":"### Foundations to learn (/teach-checked)\n- [ ] Exact algorithms — B&B, DP, ILP/CP: baseline-setters, likely unaffordable at scale\n- [ ] Metaheuristic patterns — map SA/tabu/EA onto the methods under test\n- [ ] Jin & Branke noise menu: resampling vs population-filter vs modified selection","x":-350,"y":1280,"width":560,"height":200},
		{"id":"d1","type":"text","text":"## 🟧 D · Reading programme — *by project impact*\n### Tier 1 · sets the experiment frame\n**Five-paper path (in order)**\n- [ ] PSRO → [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.00832) — framework under SP/FP/DO\n- [ ] α-Rank → [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.01373) + *Spinning Tops*\n- [ ] PokéChamp → [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.04094)\n✅ VGC-Bench · - [ ] Metamon → [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.04395)\n**RLVG workshop**\n- [ ] FootsiesGym — HIGH, arm-ranking template *(protocol used by B3)*\n- [ ] Generals.io — MED\n**Self-play background** ([[Why Self-Play is consider Multi-Agent]])\n- [ ] Zhang 2024 survey §3.2–3.3 · Lanctot PSRO","x":450,"y":160,"width":560,"height":420,"color":"2"},
